# Example policy for render offload: Intel Iris Xe (WhateverXe) drives the display
# and desktop, NVIDIA (e.g. RTX 4050) is a headless Metal device for heavy apps/games.
#
# Install as: /Library/GPUBundles/nvmtl-gpu-policy.txt
# The plugin reads it when nmhybrid>0 or debug.nvaccel_headless>0 and another
# Metal GPU is present. It must be a regular file owned by root and not writable
# by group/others (like the DLSS cache policy).
#
# In headless+iGPU setups with no policy file, the driver defaults to "mode apple"
# and keeps built-in macOS desktop/UI processes on the integrated GPU, so most
# desktop work stays on Iris Xe and heavy apps can use NVIDIA.
#
# mode apple  # optional: follow NSSupportsAutomaticGraphicsSwitching
#
# Force specific apps onto NVIDIA (process name as seen in logs/Activity Monitor):
# nvidia Blender
# nvidia Cyberpunk2077
# nvidia <YourGameProcessName>
#
# Force specific apps to stay on Iris Xe:
# igpu Safari
# igpu firefox
